# .shai-hulud-allow — grep -E regexes matched against "path:line:content"
# hits. A matching hit is IGNORED, so keep every entry as narrow as the fact
# it records. Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

# ccxt ships Binance's OFFICIAL BSC RPC endpoint in its prediction-market
# module. TIER2 lists bsc-dataseed as a drainer C2/RPC host, so ordinary
# exchange-library data reads as an IoC. Introduced in ccxt 4.5.68; 4.5.43
# does not contain it, which is the only reason market-maker-bot passed while
# tokenbot-cli failed. Scoped to the ccxt path AND that one hostname: any
# other marker in ccxt source still fails.
^\./node_modules/ccxt/.*bsc-dataseed\.binance\.org

# The same data also appears in ccxt's prebuilt browser bundle and its
# sourcemap. Those are SINGLE-LINE minified files, and the scanner truncates
# each hit to 240 characters, so the hostname is cut away and a
# content-scoped rule can never match them. These two must therefore be
# matched by PATH.
#
# COST, stated plainly: a marker injected ONLY into these two generated
# artifacts would be missed. Accepted because both are built from
# ccxt/js/src, which IS still scanned in full, so a compromised ccxt has to
# evade the source scan as well. Do not extend path-scoping past these two
# files.
^\./node_modules/ccxt/dist/ccxt\.browser\.min\.js:
^\./node_modules/ccxt/dist/ccxt\.browser\.min\.js\.map:
